417] [17592186533972 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $c(n)$ be a cost for option $n,$ where $n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}.$ We want to write the optimal option $\\overset{^}{n}$ as \"the value of $n$ that makes $c(n)$ as small as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{n}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533972 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "00fdbc42-937e-5a35-be79-3ffa566504b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533972 #edb/ref 1074 "We want $\\overset{^}{n}$ to be an *input value* $n$ where the cost $c(n)$ is as small as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡min$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{n}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}}c(n).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-355401" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533975 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533975 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $w(y)$ be a weight for node $y,$ where $y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}.$ We want to write the selected node $\\overset{^}{y}$ as \"the value of $y$ that makes $w(y)$ as large as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{y}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0e94aa36-f8ac-5d68-8a85-88c135136bde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186533975 #edb/ref 1074 "We want $\\overset{^}{y}$ to be an *input value* $y$ where the weight $w(y)$ is as large as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡max$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{y\\in \\{-7,-5,-3,-1\\}}w(y).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534007 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534007 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534007 #edb/ref 1069 "q-355387" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534007 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534007 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B=\\{-4,-2,0,3\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nk(-4)=-5,\\,k(-2)=-8,\\,k(0)=-2,\\,k(3)=-8.\n$$\n\nCompute ${min}_{x\\in B}k(x)$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in B}k(x).$\n\n$\\,$\n${min}_{x\\in B}k(x)=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in B}k(x)=$ {{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534007 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53479689-99f5-53fc-9bbf-170474b20c8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534007 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${min}_{x\\in B}k(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in B}k(x)$ is an input in $B$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $-5,$ $-8,$ $-2,$ and $-8,$ so the minimum output value is $-8.$ This minimum occurs at both $x=-2$ and $x=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{min}_{x\\in B}k(x)=-8\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in B}k(x)=\\{-2,3\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534017 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534017 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534017 #edb/ref 1069 "q-355275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534017 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534017 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $S=\\{-4,1,3,7\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(-4)=5,\\,f(1)=-2,\\,f(3)=5,\\,f(7)=3.\n$$\n\nCompute ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x).$\n\n$\\,$\n${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$ {{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534017 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b85f086-3ff0-5996-862a-13fba81da102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534017 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nThe outputs are $5,$ $-2,$ $5,$ and $3,$ so the maximum output value is $5.$ This maximum occurs at both $x=-4$ and $x=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=5\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=\\{-4,3\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-355268" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $S=\\{-2,0,1,4\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nh(-2)=3,\\,h(0)=7,\\,h(1)=-5,\\,h(4)=2.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-4}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534019 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nHere, the outputs are $3,7,-5,$ and $2.$ \n\n- The largest output is $7,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$\n\n- The smallest output is $-5,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534055 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186533778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534055 #edb/ref 1069 "q-355392" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534055 #edb/ref